---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="physics"
  title="Phonons"
  description="Nothing here knows what a wave is. Every mass obeys Hooke's law and pulls only on its four neighbours. Out of that comes a pulse that travels, at a speed nobody wrote down, and a shortest possible wavelength that no continuous material would ever have."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="ph" class="ph-canvas" width="900" height="660"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Strike again</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Excitation</label>
        <div class="seg" id="exc">
          <button data-e="pulse" class="active">Tap</button>
          <button data-e="wave">Plane wave</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="lamctl">
        <label>Wavelength λ <b id="lamval">12.0 a</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="lam" min="1" max="24" step="1" value="4" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>48a, long</span><span>2a, the limit</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Grid <b id="nval">48 × 48</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="n" min="24" max="80" step="8" value="48" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>coarse</span><span>fine</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control"><label>Spring stiffness k <b id="kval">1.00</b></label><input type="range" id="k" min="0.2" max="4" step="0.05" value="1" /></div>
      <div class="control"><label>Mass m <b id="mval">1.00</b></label><input type="range" id="m" min="0.2" max="4" step="0.05" value="1" /></div>
      <div class="control"><label>Time rate <b id="rval">1.0×</b></label><input type="range" id="rate" min="10" max="200" value="100" /></div>

      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="follow" checked /> Follow one mass</label>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span>Sound speed a√(k/m)</span><b id="c">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Measured crest speed</span><b id="cmeas">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Frequency ω (lattice)</span><b id="w">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>ω if it were continuous</span><b id="wc">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Group velocity</span><b id="vg">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Highest ω the grid allows</span><b id="wmax">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Followed mass: now</span><b id="un">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Followed mass: net drift</span><b id="ud">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        Drag to orbit. Each line is one spring, each crossing one mass, and a
        mass only ever feels its four neighbours. The grid wraps around at the
        edges, so nothing reflects.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Tap it and watch the ring spread. Now ignore the ring and stare at the
      single highlighted mass: it bobs up, comes back down, and stops roughly
      where it began. Its <b>net drift stays near zero</b> while the pulse
      crosses the whole grid. The wave travels; the matter does not. A wave is a
      pattern moving through stuff, not stuff moving.
    </li>
    <li>
      Stiffen the springs and the pulse speeds up. Make the masses heavier and it
      slows down. The measured crest speed tracks <b>a√(k/m)</b> the whole way,
      and yet no rule in this simulation mentions a speed. Every spring only
      knows how hard to pull. Sound is what a lattice does, not something added
      to it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Double k and double m together: nothing changes. Only the <b>ratio</b>
      matters, which is why stiff light materials carry sound fast (steel, about
      5 km/s) and soft heavy ones carry it slowly (lead, about 1.2 km/s).
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch to a plane wave with a long wavelength. Its dot sits right on the
      dashed straight line, the continuum prediction, and it rides at exactly c.
      Now shorten the wavelength. The lattice curve <b>bends away below the
      line</b>, and the wave gets slower than sound. The smooth wave equation is
      only the long-wavelength approximation of something grainy.
    </li>
    <li>
      Push the wavelength slider to its limit, λ = 2a. The wave <b>stops
      travelling altogether</b>: group velocity zero, just a standing shudder at
      the highest frequency the grid can carry. There is a ceiling frequency, and
      it exists purely because matter comes in lumps. In a real crystal that
      ceiling is a few terahertz, and it is why solids stop conducting sound
      above it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Try to imagine a wave shorter than 2a. Neighbouring masses are already
      alternating up, down, up, down. There is nothing left to subdivide, so
      there is no such wave. Discreteness does not just approximate the continuum
      badly at short scales, it <b>runs out of scales entirely</b>.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas } from '../../../lib/sim';
  import { equationBar } from '../../../lib/equation';

  // Lattice spacing a = 1. Out-of-plane displacement u, so this is the scalar
  // wave equation on a grid: m ü = k Σ_neighbours (u_nb − u).
  let N = 48;                                  // masses per side
  const state = {
    exc: 'pulse' as 'pulse' | 'wave',
    n: 4,        // whole wavelengths across the box, so λ = N/n
    k: 1,
    m: 1,
    rate: 1,
    running: true,
    follow: true,
    yaw: 0.62,
    pitch: -0.58,
  };
  let u = new Float64Array(N * N);
  let v = new Float64Array(N * N);
  let TRACK = 0;            // the followed mass, ~21% of the grid off centre
  let rMin = 7, rMax = 20;  // radii between which the crest speed is fitted

  /** Resize every per-site buffer after the grid resolution changes. */
  function allocate() {
    u = new Float64Array(N * N);
    v = new Float64Array(N * N);
    px = new Float64Array(N * N);
    py = new Float64Array(N * N);
    okp = new Uint8Array(N * N);
    TRACK = (N / 2) * N + (N / 2 + Math.round(N * 0.21));
    // Fit the crest between these radii: far enough out that the tap has
    // organised itself, well short of N/2 where the wrap-around wave meets it
    // head on. Below N = 40 no such window exists and the fit is unusable.
    rMin = Math.max(4, Math.round(N * 0.18));
    rMax = Math.round(N * 0.34);
  }

  const s = () => state.k / state.m;         // only the ratio matters
  const cSound = () => Math.sqrt(s());
  const lambda = () => N / state.n;
  const kWave = () => (2 * Math.PI * state.n) / N;
  const omegaLattice = () => 2 * Math.sqrt(s()) * Math.abs(Math.sin(kWave() / 2));
  const omegaMax = () => 2 * Math.sqrt(s());
  const vGroup = () => Math.sqrt(s()) * Math.cos(kWave() / 2);

  let trace: number[] = [];
  let driftSum = 0, driftN = 0;
  // running least squares for the crest speed, r = speed · t
  let cn = 0, cSt = 0, cSr = 0, cStt = 0, cStr = 0, crestDone = false, crestSpeed = NaN, crestMaxR = 0;
  let simTime = 0;

  function excite() {
    u.fill(0);
    v.fill(0);
    trace = [];
    driftSum = 0;
    driftN = 0;
    cn = cSt = cSr = cStt = cStr = 0;
    crestDone = false;
    crestSpeed = NaN;
    crestMaxR = 0;
    simTime = 0;
    if (state.exc === 'pulse') {
      // σ = 2.5 keeps the tap dominated by long wavelengths, so its crest
      // really does travel at the sound speed rather than lagging.
      const cx = N / 2, cy = N / 2, sig = 2.5;
      for (let j = 0; j < N; j++)
        for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
          const dx = i - cx, dy = j - cy;
          u[j * N + i] = Math.exp(-(dx * dx + dy * dy) / (2 * sig * sig));
        }
      // Remove the uniform part. Σu is conserved on a periodic grid, so any
      // offset would be a permanent lift of the whole sheet, which is not a
      // wave at all and would show up as a fake drift on the followed mass.
      let mean = 0;
      for (let c = 0; c < N * N; c++) mean += u[c];
      mean /= N * N;
      for (let c = 0; c < N * N; c++) u[c] -= mean;
    } else {
      const kx = kWave(), w = omegaLattice(), A = 0.55;
      for (let j = 0; j < N; j++)
        for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
          u[j * N + i] = A * Math.cos(kx * i);
          v[j * N + i] = A * w * Math.sin(kx * i); // travelling, not standing
        }
    }
  }

  function physics(dtFrame: number) {
    const sr = s();
    const dtMax = 0.25 / Math.sqrt(8 * sr); // symplectic Euler stability margin
    const sub = Math.min(32, Math.max(1, Math.ceil(dtFrame / dtMax)));
    const dt = dtFrame / sub;
    for (let step = 0; step < sub; step++) {
      for (let j = 0; j < N; j++) {
        const jm = ((j - 1 + N) % N) * N, jp = ((j + 1) % N) * N, j0 = j * N;
        for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
          const c = j0 + i;
          const lap = u[j0 + ((i + 1) % N)] + u[j0 + ((i - 1 + N) % N)] + u[jp + i] + u[jm + i] - 4 * u[c];
          v[c] += sr * lap * dt;
        }
      }
      for (let c = 0; c < N * N; c++) u[c] += v[c] * dt;
      simTime += dt;
      trackCrest();
    }
  }

  /** Follow the radius of the outgoing crest and fit r = speed · t. */
  function trackCrest() {
    if (state.exc !== 'pulse' || crestDone) return;
    const row = (N / 2) * N, cx = N / 2;
    let best = 0, peak = 0;
    for (let d = 2; d < N / 2 - 3; d++) {
      const a = Math.abs(u[row + cx + d]);
      if (a > best) { best = a; peak = d; }
    }
    // Sub-site position of the crest by parabolic fit, otherwise the integer
    // site index quantises the fit badly over the short measuring window.
    let bi = peak;
    if (peak >= 3 && peak <= N / 2 - 5) {
      const a = Math.abs(u[row + cx + peak - 1]);
      const b = Math.abs(u[row + cx + peak]);
      const c2 = Math.abs(u[row + cx + peak + 1]);
      const den = a - 2 * b + c2;
      if (den < -1e-12) bi = peak + (0.5 * (a - c2)) / den;
    }
    // Stop once the ring leaves the window. On a periodic grid it wraps back
    // in, and those return visits would drag the fitted slope towards zero.
    if (bi > rMax || (cn > 12 && bi < crestMaxR - 2)) { crestDone = cn > 8; return; }
    // Start past the radius where the tap is still organising itself.
    if (bi < rMin) return;
    if (bi > crestMaxR) crestMaxR = bi;
    cn++;
    cSt += simTime;
    cSr += bi;
    cStt += simTime * simTime;
    cStr += simTime * bi;
    if (cn > 8) {
      const den = cn * cStt - cSt * cSt;
      if (Math.abs(den) > 1e-9) crestSpeed = (cn * cStr - cSt * cSr) / den;
    }
  }

  // --- canvas --------------------------------------------------------------
  const canvas = document.getElementById('ph') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => {});
  const css = (v2: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(v2).trim();
  const ink = () => css('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
  const ACC = '#7c8cff', WARM = '#f59e0b';

  const CX = 450, CY = 258, CAM = 3.2, FOCAL = 2.7, SCALE = 232, HEIGHT = 0.34;
  const DISP = { x: 44, y: 532, w: 366, h: 96 };
  const TR = { x: 492, y: 532, w: 366, h: 96 };

  function project(x: number, y: number, z: number) {
    const cy = Math.cos(state.yaw), sy = Math.sin(state.yaw);
    const cp = Math.cos(state.pitch), sp = Math.sin(state.pitch);
    const x1 = x * cy + z * sy;
    const z1 = -x * sy + z * cy;
    const y2 = y * cp - z1 * sp;
    const z2 = y * sp + z1 * cp;
    const zc = z2 + CAM;
    const sc = FOCAL / Math.max(0.05, zc);
    return { sx: CX + x1 * sc * SCALE, sy: CY - y2 * sc * SCALE, zc };
  }

  const LEVELS = 9;
  let px = new Float64Array(N * N), py = new Float64Array(N * N);
  let okp = new Uint8Array(N * N);
  const paths: Path2D[] = [];

  function levelColor(l: number) {
    const t = (l / (LEVELS - 1)) * 2 - 1;
    const a = Math.abs(t);
    if (a < 0.12) return `rgba(${ink()},0.16)`;
    const col = t < 0 ? '124,140,255' : '245,158,11';
    return `rgba(${col},${(0.28 + 0.62 * a).toFixed(3)})`;
  }
  const bucket = (val: number) => {
    const t = Math.tanh(val / 0.5);
    return Math.max(0, Math.min(LEVELS - 1, Math.round(((t + 1) / 2) * (LEVELS - 1))));
  };

  function drawSheet() {
    for (let j = 0; j < N; j++)
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        const d = j * N + i;
        const x = (i / (N - 1)) * 2 - 1;
        const z = (j / (N - 1)) * 2 - 1;
        const p = project(x, u[d] * HEIGHT, z);
        px[d] = p.sx;
        py[d] = p.sy;
        okp[d] = p.zc > 0.1 ? 1 : 0;
      }
    for (let l = 0; l < LEVELS; l++) paths[l] = new Path2D();
    // every segment is one spring
    for (let j = 0; j < N; j++)
      for (let i = 0; i < N - 1; i++) {
        const a = j * N + i, b = a + 1;
        if (!okp[a] || !okp[b]) continue;
        const p = paths[bucket((u[a] + u[b]) / 2)];
        p.moveTo(px[a], py[a]);
        p.lineTo(px[b], py[b]);
      }
    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++)
      for (let j = 0; j < N - 1; j++) {
        const a = j * N + i, b = a + N;
        if (!okp[a] || !okp[b]) continue;
        const p = paths[bucket((u[a] + u[b]) / 2)];
        p.moveTo(px[a], py[a]);
        p.lineTo(px[b], py[b]);
      }
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    for (let l = 0; l < LEVELS; l++) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = levelColor(l);
      ctx.stroke(paths[l]);
    }

    if (state.follow && okp[TRACK]) {
      const i = TRACK % N, j = (TRACK / N) | 0;
      const x = (i / (N - 1)) * 2 - 1, z = (j / (N - 1)) * 2 - 1;
      const rest = project(x, 0, z);
      // stem from the rest position up to where the mass actually is
      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.45)`;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(rest.sx, rest.sy);
      ctx.lineTo(px[TRACK], py[TRACK]);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.35)`;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(rest.sx, rest.sy, 3.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';
      ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(10,11,14,0.8)';
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(px[TRACK], py[TRACK], 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.stroke();
    }
  }

  function label(text: string, x: number, y: number, alpha = 0.55, align: CanvasTextAlign = 'left', size = 12) {
    ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${ink()},${alpha})`;
    ctx.font = `${size}px ui-monospace, monospace`;
    ctx.textAlign = align;
    ctx.fillText(text, x, y);
    ctx.textAlign = 'left';
  }

  function drawDispersion() {
    const wmax = omegaMax();
    const X = (kk: number) => DISP.x + (kk / Math.PI) * DISP.w;
    const Y = (w: number) => DISP.y + DISP.h - Math.min(1, w / (wmax * 1.15)) * DISP.h;
    label('WHICH WAVES THE GRID ALLOWS   ω vs k', DISP.x, DISP.y - 12, 0.5);

    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.25)`;
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(DISP.x, DISP.y + DISP.h);
    ctx.lineTo(DISP.x + DISP.w, DISP.y + DISP.h);
    ctx.moveTo(DISP.x, DISP.y);
    ctx.lineTo(DISP.x, DISP.y + DISP.h);
    ctx.stroke();

    // what a perfectly continuous sheet would do: ω = c k, a straight line
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.4)`;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(X(0), Y(0));
    let done = false;
    for (let i = 1; i <= 60 && !done; i++) {
      const kk = (Math.PI * i) / 60, w = cSound() * kk;
      if (w > wmax * 1.15) done = true;
      ctx.lineTo(X(kk), Y(w));
    }
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);

    ctx.strokeStyle = WARM;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let i = 0; i <= 90; i++) {
      const kk = (Math.PI * i) / 90;
      const w = 2 * Math.sqrt(s()) * Math.abs(Math.sin(kk / 2));
      i ? ctx.lineTo(X(kk), Y(w)) : ctx.moveTo(X(kk), Y(w));
    }
    ctx.stroke();

    if (state.exc === 'wave') {
      ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(X(kWave()), Y(omegaLattice()), 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    }
    label('continuum', X(Math.PI * 0.42), Y(cSound() * Math.PI * 0.42) - 8, 0.4, 'left', 10);
    label('lattice', X(Math.PI * 0.8), Y(2 * Math.sqrt(s()) * Math.abs(Math.sin(Math.PI * 0.4))) + 14, 0.5, 'left', 10);
    label('k = π/a', X(Math.PI), DISP.y + DISP.h + 15, 0.4, 'right', 11);
    label('λ = 2a', X(Math.PI), DISP.y + DISP.h + 27, 0.3, 'right', 10);
    label('long waves', DISP.x + 2, DISP.y + DISP.h + 15, 0.35, 'left', 11);
    label(`ω_max = ${wmax.toFixed(2)}`, DISP.x + DISP.w, DISP.y - 12, 0.4, 'right', 11);
  }

  function drawTrace() {
    label('THE FOLLOWED MASS, over time', TR.x, TR.y - 12, 0.5);
    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.25)`;
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(TR.x, TR.y + TR.h / 2);
    ctx.lineTo(TR.x + TR.w, TR.y + TR.h / 2);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    if (trace.length > 1) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let i = 0; i < trace.length; i++) {
        const x = TR.x + (TR.w * i) / (trace.length - 1);
        const y = TR.y + TR.h / 2 - Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, trace[i])) * (TR.h / 2 - 4);
        i ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    label('rest position', TR.x + 4, TR.y + TR.h / 2 - 5, 0.3, 'left', 10);
    label('it returns to where it started', TR.x + TR.w, TR.y + TR.h + 15, 0.35, 'right', 11);
  }

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    drawSheet();
    drawDispersion();
    drawTrace();
  }

  // --- readouts ------------------------------------------------------------
  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setEq = equationBar();
  function updateReadout() {
    el('c').textContent = cSound().toFixed(3);
    el('cmeas').textContent =
      state.exc !== 'pulse' ? 'tap mode only'
      : N < 40 ? 'grid too coarse'
      : isNaN(crestSpeed) ? 'measuring…'
      : crestSpeed.toFixed(3);
    el('w').textContent = state.exc === 'wave' ? omegaLattice().toFixed(3) : '—';
    el('wc').textContent = state.exc === 'wave' ? (cSound() * kWave()).toFixed(3) : '—';
    el('vg').textContent = state.exc === 'wave' ? vGroup().toFixed(3) : '—';
    el('wmax').textContent = omegaMax().toFixed(3);
    el('un').textContent = u[TRACK].toFixed(3);
    el('ud').textContent = driftN ? (driftSum / driftN).toFixed(4) : '—';
    setEq([
      [
        ['\\omega(k) = 2\\sqrt{K/m}\\,\\big|\\sin(ka/2)\\big|', ACC],
        '\\quad\\text{not}',
        ['\\omega = c\\,k', WARM],
      ],
      [
        `c = a\\sqrt{K/m} = ${cSound().toFixed(3)}`,
        [`\\quad\\omega = ${state.exc === 'wave' ? omegaLattice().toFixed(3) : '\\text{--}'}`, ACC],
        [`\\quad c\\,k = ${state.exc === 'wave' ? (cSound() * kWave()).toFixed(3) : '\\text{--}'}`, WARM],
        `\\quad\\omega_{\\max} = ${omegaMax().toFixed(3)}`,
      ],
      [
        'long waves cannot tell the lattice from a continuum; short ones can, and they run slower',
      ],
    ]);
  }

  // --- loop ----------------------------------------------------------------
  function frame() {
    if (state.running) {
      physics(0.5 * state.rate);
      trace.push(u[TRACK]);
      if (trace.length > 360) trace.shift();
      driftSum += u[TRACK];
      driftN++;
    }
    draw();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls ------------------------------------------------------------
  let dragging = false, lx = 0, ly = 0;
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
    dragging = true; lx = e.clientX; ly = e.clientY;
    canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
  });
  canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {
    if (!dragging) return;
    state.yaw += (e.clientX - lx) * 0.01;
    state.pitch = Math.max(-1.4, Math.min(-0.06, state.pitch + (e.clientY - ly) * 0.01));
    lx = e.clientX; ly = e.clientY;
  });
  const stop = () => (dragging = false);
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', stop);
  canvas.addEventListener('pointercancel', stop);

  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', excite);

  const lamCtl = el('lamctl');
  function syncLam() {
    lamCtl.style.opacity = state.exc === 'wave' ? '1' : '0.4';
    (el('lam') as HTMLInputElement).disabled = state.exc !== 'wave';
    el('lamval').textContent = `${lambda().toFixed(1)} a`;
  }
  el('exc').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#exc button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.exc = btn.dataset.e as 'pulse' | 'wave';
    syncLam();
    excite();
  });
  (el('lam') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    state.n = +(e.target as HTMLInputElement).value;
    syncLam();
    excite();
  });
  const nEl = el('n') as HTMLInputElement;
  const lamEl = el('lam') as HTMLInputElement;
  function syncGrid() {
    el('nval').textContent = `${N} × ${N}`;
    // λ = N/n, so the shortest wave is always 2a but the slider's reach changes
    lamEl.max = String(N / 2);
    if (state.n > N / 2) state.n = N / 2;
    lamEl.value = String(state.n);
    const hint = lamEl.parentElement!.querySelector('.scale-hint');
    if (hint) hint.innerHTML = `<span>${N}a, long</span><span>2a, the limit</span>`;
  }
  nEl.addEventListener('input', () => {
    N = +nEl.value;
    allocate();
    syncGrid();
    syncLam();
    excite();
  });

  const bind = (id: string, key: 'k' | 'm', after?: () => void) => {
    const inp = el(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    inp.addEventListener('input', () => {
      state[key] = +inp.value;
      el(id + 'val').textContent = state[key].toFixed(2);
      after?.();
    });
  };
  bind('k', 'k', excite);
  bind('m', 'm', excite);
  (el('rate') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    state.rate = +(e.target as HTMLInputElement).value / 100;
    el('rval').textContent = `${state.rate.toFixed(1)}×`;
  });
  (el('follow') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.follow = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
  });

  allocate();
  syncGrid();
  syncLam();
  excite();
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

<style>
  .ph-canvas {
    cursor: grab;
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .ph-canvas:active {
    cursor: grabbing;
  }
  .scale-hint {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
</style>
